														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2173118">
									

<p>What's with everyone hating on D-Class termination all of a sudden? It's such an established piece of the universe that complaining about it is on par with complaining about the existence of SCP-682, the Overseers, or Clef&#8230;</p>
<p>You don't have to use 'em, but why on earth would you go out of your way to object to referencing a thing that ~99% of the site generally includes in their headcanon, if not directly into their stories or articles?</p>
<p>Also, if we're going to worry about being gay-inclusive for a 2-person sample set, shouldn't we include a whole collapsible dedicated to letting a bunch of D-Class escape, since knowing how it impacts all possible flavors of sexuality is obviously more important than little things like operational security?</p>
<p>&#8230;Okay, that was pretty sarcastic, but from a scientific standpoint they only have data on two couples escaping. They don't <em>know</em> how it will affect different sexual preferences, so why would they worry about being politically correct? That just removes a data point. The two couples were straight. They wrote that down and didn't test it further because, y'know, the D-Class escaped. That's probably not something they want to encourage.</p>

							</div>

								
