			<div class="content" id="post-content-2168090">
									

<p>You literally had my upvote immediately upon reaching the coloring book- paused reading, scolled up, and hit the button then and there.</p>
<p>I totally got the &quot;some sort of shop class for magical entities&quot; thing- I was thinking school for the dark arts, but the basic idea totally telegraphed for me.</p>
<p>I can just picture the instructor's commentary on some of these&#8230;</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>The telephone:</strong> Highly derivative. Even the mortals are using this one lately. Nonetheless, A'fjrgl as always demonstrates strong technical execution.</li>
<li><strong>the ash tray:</strong> Effect's intent and execution commendable. C- for unintentionally curing smoking habit and poor craftsmanship.</li>
<li><strong>The birdhouse:</strong> Gxrydr tries very hard.</li>
<li><strong>Lamp:</strong> Absolutely infuriating- conceptually excellent. However, I am disappointed by the use of a mortal-crafted lamp (this is a <em>shop</em> class, after all), and the effect could be easily replicated by mortal technology.</li>
<li><strong>Bookends:</strong> More &quot;inconvinient&quot; than &quot;cursed&quot;. Also, they slide when holding large tomes.</li>
<li><strong>Cuckoo Clock:</strong> Vrtyi reminds me why I became a teacher.</li>
<li><strong>The Coloring Book:</strong> I grow increasingly uncertain whether Cthythrea is a tragically gifted idiot or a true genius: I suspect this giggling ninny may be attempting to drive me toward a mental breakdown. <em>Hereby leaving directions for my successor to revise grades on all projects to A+ if she is successful.</em></li>
</ul>
<p>Edit: Updated and expanded on a whim.</p>

