			<div class="content" id="post-content-2168153">
									

<p><strong>this pleases me greatly</strong></p>
<p>I don't even need the backstory. I just love that it's a weird place that does weird things and that is has all the trappings of a horror story where the community knows something bad is going on but participates in covering it up as best they can.</p>
<p><em>&quot;Naw you don't want to go to that shop. It's a bad shop,&quot; said the old feller, who stared at you with narrow eyes when you went in there anyway.</em></p>
<p>Good lord I even buy them noticing that a group moved in to help steer people away and not making a big deal about it. This is so good.</p>
<p><em>&quot;Yeah them gov'ment fellas finally got wind about the bad shop we don't talk about. But don't say anything. This's top secret, yaknow.&quot; *wink*</em></p>
<p>edit: I even love that with the secret backstory, there's no need for the demonic flea market to give a crap about being contained, they just need to get rid of these class projects and the Foundation is happy to scoop them up straight into containment. Everything about this is my favorite flavor of lighthearted Foundation. All the scare is there for you to assemble yourself in your head if you wish, by dreaming up some poor sod who gets an A+ project.</p>
<p>edit2: <em>&quot;I tried to warn them, I looked them straight in the eye and said 'That there is a devil's shop, friend. Everything you can buy in there is cursed and will come after you like something out of a Stephen King book, only one of his crappy newer ones,' but that guy just said 'Cool!' and went right in. Now he has a clock that won't stop screaming.&quot;</em></p>
<p><em>&quot;It's not all bad, you hear about that one guy who came back with his new wife? Said they got a lucky coloring book that saved them from some men in black types. They came back to buy something else and it cured their smoking!&quot;</em></p>
<p><em>&quot;What, really? Maybe I should go give that place a try myself.&quot;</em></p>
<p>And then a very patient demon got an A+</p>

