			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2168481">
									

<p>I originally named him Mr. Elder, but that seemed too spot on. I changed it to &quot;anziano&quot; which Google Translate says is Italian for &quot;elder.&quot; It's not ideal. I'm open to other suggestions for the name.</p>
<p>Would it help if he referred to the items as &quot;projects&quot;? Would that be a clue that's not too much of a clue?</p>
<p>Dammit, you're right about the bookends. Let me think about how to change it.</p>
<p>The effects of the coloring book need to be over the top to really drive home the point that this student completely missed the concept of &quot;cursed object&quot; by the widest margin possible.</p>
<p>EDIT: Would it be more or less confusing if the log entries for the individual items said &quot;<strong>Grade:</strong> Gamal-minus&quot; instead of &quot;<strong>Glyph:</strong> Gamal-minus&quot;?</p>

